                "xpath": "/html[1]/body[1]/div[4]/div[2]/div[1]/div[12]/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]",
                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Gimel hebrew letter icon Stock Vector Image &amp; Art - Alamy](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110522-2762-0139-0000-df56fb4c6020:4)\nGimmel (also spelled **Gimel** , letter **ג** ) is the third letter of the Hebrew alphabet, detailed on the [Chabad Gimmel Guide](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137075/jewish/Gimmel.htm).[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137075/jewish/Gimmel.htm)\n\n### Key Facts\n\n- **Letter and Symbol:** ג\n- **Numerical Value:** 3\n- **Sound:** \"G\" as in \"girl\"\n- **Name Meaning:** Traditionally tied to *gamal* (camel), *gemul* (reward/recompense), and the act of weaning or nourishing.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137075/jewish/Gimmel.htm)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9JWCZgLNUnw)[[3]](https://mazorbooks.wordpress.com/2020/10/07/gimel/)[[4]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=06kaFTl542U)[[5]](https://inner.org/hebleter/gimmel.htm)[[6]](https://www.chabad.org/kabbalah/article_cdo/aid/380533/jewish/The-Letter-Gimel.htm)\n\n### Symbolic Meaning\n\n- **The Benefactor:** In Jewish tradition and the Talmud, the shape of the gimmel resembles a person walking or a rich person running to give charity (*tzedakah* ) to a poor person (represented by the next letter, Dalet).[[1]](https://inner.org/hebleter/gimmel.htm)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137075/jewish/Gimmel.htm)\n- **Structure:** It is formed by a vertical line (*vav* ) with a small foot (*yud* ) at the bottom, symbolizing a person in motion stepping forward to help others.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/kabbalah/article_cdo/aid/380533/jewish/The-Letter-Gimel.htm)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137075/jewish/Gimmel.htm)\n- **Completeness:** The number three represents stability, the three Patriarchs (Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob), and the connection between the Creator and creation.[[1]](https://hebrewtoday.com/alphabet/the-hebrew-letter-gimel-%D7%92/)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=06kaFTl542U)[[3]](https://www.chabad.org/kabbalah/article_cdo/aid/380533/jewish/The-Letter-Gimel.htm)\n\nWould you like to learn about the **next letter (Dalet)** or see examples of **Hebrew words** that start with Gimmel?",
